    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Please run DRAGON to build one joint network between plasma proteins and stool metabolites for our IBD project. Each table has sample IDs in the first column and continuous values. I can't remember whether the metabolomics was run on the same patients as the proteomics or on a separate recruitment wave."
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Before I choose a workflow, please tell me:\n- Were the metabolomics and proteomics run on the same patients?\n  You wrote: \"I can't remember whether the metabolomics was run on the same patients as the proteomics or on a separate recruitment wave\". DRAGON's contract: \"DRAGON consumes exactly two paired sample-by-feature continuous omics tables and produces one aggregate undirected multi-omic network\".\n\nNo workflow has been selected and nothing runs before you answer.\n\nNo files were inspected and no analysis ran."
    },
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Previous NetZoo goal: Please run DRAGON to build one joint network between plasma proteins and stool metabolites for our IBD project. Each table has sample IDs in the first column and continuous values. I can't remember whether the metabolomics was run on the same patients as the proteomics or on a separate recruitment wave.\nUser follow-up: They are two separate groups of patients."
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "What I understood you are asking for:\n1. \"Please run DRAGON to build one joint network between plasma proteins and stool metabolites for our IBD project.\" -- I couldn't match this to anything a registered NetZoo workflow produces or lets you set. DRAGON gives: one undirected partial-correlation network within and between two matched omics layers (any two, e.g. expression and methylation), across all samples. A p-value and a Benjamini-Hochberg adjusted p-value for every edge (adjusted within each layer and across the layers), to filter edges by significance.\n\nI couldn't match this to a result any registered NetZoo workflow produces, so none is offered.\n\nNo files were inspected and no analysis ran."
    }
